<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - June 10.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to watch - June 10.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- Continental Airlines is expected to buy 35 wide-body jets as part of an exclusive deal with Boeing Co, the New York Times reported.</p>
<p>-- Xylan Corp said it expects second-quarter revenues and earnings to fall below results of the first quarter.</p>
<p>-- Whole Foods Market Inc said it agreed to acquire Amrion Inc for about $146 million. Whole Foods, the natural food supermarket chain, said it would take a fourth-quarter charge of $3-$5 million for the merger.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
